---
import BaseLayout from '#layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Button } from '@repo/ui';

const title = 'About - SteadyMind';
const description = 'Who is behind SteadyMind, how the coaching works, and where its limits are.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <article class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">Coaching for the ordinary hard parts</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground mb-10">
      SteadyMind exists for the stretch between "fine" and "needs a clinic": the months of bad sleep, the low hum of worry, the job that takes more than it gives. Most people there do not need treatment. They need a plan, a pace, and someone to check in.
    </p>

    <div class="space-y-8 leading-relaxed">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">How the coaching works</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Every programme is built the same way: a short daily lesson, one practice to try, and a weekly review that asks what actually changed. The techniques come from cognitive behavioural coaching, sleep science, and acceptance-based approaches, chosen because they have held up in trials and in practice. Nothing here depends on willpower alone.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Who it is for</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          People who are functioning but tired of it costing so much. Managers who cannot switch off. New parents who have forgotten what rest feels like. Anyone who has read about anxiety and wants a structured way to work on it rather than another article.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-3">Where the limits are</h2>
        <p class="text-muted-foreground">
          Coaching is not therapy and not medical care. If you have a diagnosis, are on medication, or are in crisis, SteadyMind is a companion to professional support, not a replacement for it. When a coach sees something outside their scope, they say so and help you find the right place.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
      <Button size="lg" asChild><a href="/courses">See programmes</a></Button>
      <Button size="lg" variant="outline" asChild><a href="/pricing">Pricing</a></Button>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
